WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.232 --> 00:00:02.828
- My first guest's voice
is incredibly heavy.

00:00:02.828 --> 00:00:04.338
That's only 'cause it's made of pure gold.

00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:05.873
See what we did there
with that little dad joke?

00:00:05.873 --> 00:00:06.706
You're welcome.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.922
He's got a new album called "Harmony,"

00:00:08.922 --> 00:00:11.861
and tickets are on sale for
his virtual holiday concert.

00:00:11.861 --> 00:00:14.581
Let's give it up for
Josh Groban, everybody!

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:18.498
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:00:26.645 --> 00:00:27.478
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:27.478 --> 00:00:28.311
- Hello!

00:00:28.311 --> 00:00:29.144
- Oh, wow.
- How are you?

00:00:29.144 --> 00:00:30.704
- Oh my God, not Zoom.

00:00:30.704 --> 00:00:31.794
- [Kelly] I know.

00:00:31.794 --> 00:00:32.847
- This is extraordinary.

00:00:32.847 --> 00:00:34.515
- [Kelly] This is what
it's like outside the box.

00:00:34.515 --> 00:00:36.105
- I'm loving it. This is amazing.

00:00:36.105 --> 00:00:37.068
Thank you for having me.

00:00:37.068 --> 00:00:38.413
- No, thank you for coming.

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:39.246
How are you?

00:00:39.246 --> 00:00:40.675
- I'm good. I'm here for the gift.

00:00:40.675 --> 00:00:41.748
- I'm here for the gift.

00:00:41.748 --> 00:00:43.331
- Yeah, yeah. I, just so we all know -

00:00:43.331 --> 00:00:44.164
- Well, like I mentioned before -

00:00:44.164 --> 00:00:46.498
- First and foremost, first of all,

00:00:46.498 --> 00:00:48.822
props to Edward and what he's doing, I -

00:00:48.822 --> 00:00:49.655
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:49.655 --> 00:00:51.112
- That is like my dream life.

00:00:51.112 --> 00:00:51.945
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:51.945 --> 00:00:54.746
- To just take care of
dogs and fly around.

00:00:54.746 --> 00:00:56.606
If you ever need a
theme song, let me know.

00:00:56.606 --> 00:00:57.939
- [Edward] Thank you.

00:00:57.939 --> 00:00:59.696
- Maybe, so, wait.

00:00:59.696 --> 00:01:02.558
I don't know if you've heard,
but it's almost Christmas.

00:01:02.558 --> 00:01:03.548
- [Josh] I have heard, yes.

00:01:03.548 --> 00:01:05.878
- Are you like, what's
the Groban household like?

00:01:05.878 --> 00:01:07.787
- Well, I mean, I grew up with

00:01:07.787 --> 00:01:09.516
just such magical Christmases.

00:01:09.516 --> 00:01:10.349
I was very lucky.

00:01:10.349 --> 00:01:13.182
My dad comes from a Jewish family,

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:18.137
but when he married my mom,
my mom is so Christmassy.

00:01:18.137 --> 00:01:20.795
Like, she loves putting Santas everywhere.

00:01:20.795 --> 00:01:22.314
She's got a collection
of Santas, and you know,

00:01:22.314 --> 00:01:24.841
she loves trees and decorations so much

00:01:24.841 --> 00:01:26.493
that even if there isn't room,

00:01:26.493 --> 00:01:29.443
we'll find a place for a second tree.

00:01:29.443 --> 00:01:31.978
The house growing up, smelled
like such a forest that -

00:01:31.978 --> 00:01:32.993
- Oh, they were real trees, too?

00:01:32.993 --> 00:01:34.726
- Oh, they were real trees. Oh yeah, yeah.

00:01:34.726 --> 00:01:37.244
I think there was a bird
in one of them once.

00:01:37.244 --> 00:01:39.994
Yeah. It's a whole thing, so -

00:01:39.994 --> 00:01:41.077
- Like a real bird?

00:01:41.077 --> 00:01:42.810
- Oh yeah, yeah. It was
still alive, thankfully.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.303
We cut it down and tied it to our car,

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:45.465
drove it home and then it was like

00:01:45.465 --> 00:01:46.660
(he imitates a bird call)

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.827
So, yeah, it got out okay.

00:01:49.673 --> 00:01:51.258
- But speaking of your childhood home,

00:01:51.258 --> 00:01:53.424
and just your childhood in general,

00:01:53.424 --> 00:01:55.133
you love to share throwback photos.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:56.626
So, here's one.

00:01:56.626 --> 00:01:58.237
So give me the backstory
of this little one.

00:01:58.237 --> 00:01:59.070
- [Josh] Oh, hey.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.934
- [Kelly] What's up? You are
so cute in your short shorts.

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:03.997
- [Josh] Have you done "Who
Wears Short Shorts" yet

00:02:03.997 --> 00:02:05.786
for your karaoke?

00:02:05.786 --> 00:02:07.913
That, look at those shorts, I am -

00:02:07.913 --> 00:02:08.903
- [Kelly] Those shorts are awesome.

00:02:08.903 --> 00:02:10.145
- [Josh] I'm the original Evan Hansen.

00:02:10.145 --> 00:02:11.616
Look at that arm.

00:02:11.616 --> 00:02:14.110
You know, I, that, I think
that is the exact moment

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.820
I knew that it was, the arts were for me.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.053
I think that's, you can
see the look on my face.

00:02:19.053 --> 00:02:21.856
You zoom in. You can see
the sadness behind me.

00:02:21.856 --> 00:02:22.946
- [Kelly] Oh my God, that's amazing.

00:02:22.946 --> 00:02:25.040
- [Josh] I want to be in a play so bad.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.944
- You look adorable.

00:02:26.944 --> 00:02:27.777
- [Josh] Oh, thank you.

00:02:27.777 --> 00:02:29.349
- It's so cute with the little cast.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:30.911
- Man, little Joshy on
"The Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:02:30.911 --> 00:02:31.744
Look at that.

00:02:31.744 --> 00:02:33.259
- [Kelly] It's adorable. We love kid pics.

00:02:33.259 --> 00:02:34.092
- Full circle.

00:02:34.092 --> 00:02:36.057
I just called in to apologize,

00:02:36.057 --> 00:02:39.194
mainly, because I gave all my friends

00:02:39.194 --> 00:02:42.470
your Zoom room instead of
my Zoom room by accident.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.303
- When we were you going to say,

00:02:43.303 --> 00:02:44.889
sorry for not inviting
me to your poker game?

00:02:44.889 --> 00:02:46.930
Just curious, just waiting for that one.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.082
Is it just all full, no room?

00:02:48.082 --> 00:02:49.257
- Yeah, I, you should,

00:02:49.257 --> 00:02:51.085
you should check your junk folder.

00:02:51.085 --> 00:02:52.921
I think it's probably in there somewhere.

00:02:52.921 --> 00:02:55.196
- You're so full of it, Groban.

00:02:55.196 --> 00:02:56.705
(audience applauds)

00:02:56.705 --> 00:02:57.845
All right, what's up everybody?

00:02:57.845 --> 00:02:58.908
I'm here with Josh Groban

00:02:58.908 --> 00:03:01.235
and that was a look back
at our season premier

00:03:01.235 --> 00:03:04.235
when Josh gave his friends
the wrong Zoom address

00:03:04.235 --> 00:03:06.992
for his virtual poker game, real classy.

00:03:06.992 --> 00:03:09.032
I'm still waiting on
my invite, by the way.

00:03:09.032 --> 00:03:11.251
That's fine. Do you
have poker games often?

00:03:11.251 --> 00:03:13.393
- That was my one and only poker game.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.739
I'll tell you, Kenny G plays dirty.

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:17.281
Yeah, I lost it all.

00:03:17.281 --> 00:03:20.722
I shouldn't have doubled down on jacks.

00:03:20.722 --> 00:03:21.894
I feel like that was the wrong,

00:03:21.894 --> 00:03:22.906
I was playing the wrong game.

00:03:22.906 --> 00:03:24.721
- [Kelly] Oh my God, I love you so much.

00:03:24.721 --> 00:03:26.164
- But, no, next time, of course,

00:03:26.164 --> 00:03:27.843
you're more than welcome, but -

00:03:27.843 --> 00:03:30.662
- Okay, you heard it. Y'all all heard it.

00:03:30.662 --> 00:03:31.495
- [Josh] You're in. You're in.

00:03:31.495 --> 00:03:33.545
- No, I have to ask you, have
you been doing a lot of, like,

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:34.941
I know a lot of musicians and artists

00:03:34.941 --> 00:03:36.374
have been doing virtual concerts.

00:03:36.374 --> 00:03:37.207
Have you been doing that?

00:03:37.207 --> 00:03:38.040
- Yes. Yeah.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.539
You know, when all this
started and lockdown happened,

00:03:39.539 --> 00:03:41.471
I was right at the end of a long tour.

00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:44.528
So luckily, I was about to kind
of go off cycle anyway, but,

00:03:44.528 --> 00:03:47.998
you know, all of a sudden all
that noise turns to silence.

00:03:47.998 --> 00:03:50.197
And I didn't know if it
would be the kind of thing

00:03:50.197 --> 00:03:51.498
that would feel weird or not,

00:03:51.498 --> 00:03:54.638
but to be doing these live
stream concerts has been so fun.

00:03:54.638 --> 00:03:56.842
First of all, to just
go back and, you know,

00:03:56.842 --> 00:03:58.367
put on something that's not a onesy

00:03:58.367 --> 00:03:59.776
and put my band and crew to work -

00:03:59.776 --> 00:04:00.609
- That's not pajamas.

00:04:00.609 --> 00:04:02.186
- Exactly, and get out there and sing.

00:04:02.186 --> 00:04:05.099
But also, even though there's
no applause in real time,

00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:07.413
you see, like, 85 countries
tuned in, you know,

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.818
and you see people Tweeting
you and Instagramming.

00:04:09.818 --> 00:04:10.905
We're all in a box.

00:04:10.905 --> 00:04:12.263
You know, I'm in a box doing my show,

00:04:12.263 --> 00:04:14.205
and they're in, you
know, thousands of boxes

00:04:14.205 --> 00:04:15.804
around the world and we're
feeling isolated and alone.

00:04:15.804 --> 00:04:18.444
So, to be able to do them
has just felt us feel,

00:04:18.444 --> 00:04:21.224
just made us feel just
a little more connected.

00:04:21.224 --> 00:04:22.636
- Yeah. It's really cool of you.

00:04:22.636 --> 00:04:24.427
It's a nice distraction for everyone, too.

00:04:24.427 --> 00:04:25.260
- Thanks.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.413
- And it brings hope so,
but your next concert,

00:04:27.413 --> 00:04:28.820
it's a holiday concert, right?

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:29.653
- That's right. Yeah.

00:04:29.653 --> 00:04:34.353
We're going to, my first
ever Christmas concert,

00:04:34.353 --> 00:04:35.294
on December 19th.

00:04:35.294 --> 00:04:36.162
We're, you know -

00:04:36.162 --> 00:04:36.995
- Wait, what?

00:04:36.995 --> 00:04:37.828
- I've never done, I know.

00:04:37.828 --> 00:04:41.443
I've done a ton of
Christmas songs in my life.

00:04:41.443 --> 00:04:42.955
I had pretty big Christmas album,

00:04:42.955 --> 00:04:45.272
and I've never done a full
length Christmas concert.

00:04:45.272 --> 00:04:47.376
And so, you know, what
better time than now,

00:04:47.376 --> 00:04:50.292
when we're all kind of
apart and feeling isolated

00:04:50.292 --> 00:04:52.439
during the holidays,
to do a virtual concert

00:04:52.439 --> 00:04:53.893
of the songs that have, you know,

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.278
given me so much warmth over the years.

00:04:55.278 --> 00:04:56.710
So, I'm looking forward to it, yeah.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:57.915
- [Kelly] Yeah, that's
going to be beautiful.

00:04:57.915 --> 00:04:58.835
- Maybe it'll be the first of many.

00:04:58.835 --> 00:05:00.523
- I always like to ask performers this,

00:05:00.523 --> 00:05:02.661
'cause I feel like
everybody always, you know,

00:05:02.661 --> 00:05:05.144
everybody knows I'm like
an extrovert, obviously,

00:05:05.144 --> 00:05:06.560
but I actually was quite introverted

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.755
before singing and I was very shy.

00:05:09.755 --> 00:05:11.871
We moved around a little
bit, and I was very shy.

00:05:11.871 --> 00:05:13.588
And then once I kind of found music,

00:05:13.588 --> 00:05:15.972
it kind of changed my whole personality,

00:05:15.972 --> 00:05:17.787
like my confidence, like everything.

00:05:17.787 --> 00:05:19.347
Was that, was music like that for you?

00:05:19.347 --> 00:05:20.799
- Oh, 100%.

00:05:20.799 --> 00:05:23.151
You know, having an arts
teacher to kind of pull me out

00:05:23.151 --> 00:05:25.106
from the back, where I was
kind of singing quietly,

00:05:25.106 --> 00:05:27.190
and just knew I wanted to be a part of it,

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:29.319
but didn't have the confidence
to say, hey, you know,

00:05:29.319 --> 00:05:32.494
I've got a voice, to have that moment

00:05:32.494 --> 00:05:33.739
changed everything for me

00:05:33.739 --> 00:05:36.466
because it made me realize that
I had a way to communicate.

00:05:36.466 --> 00:05:38.426
It helped my grades.

00:05:38.426 --> 00:05:41.463
And so, now I'm in a position, as are you,

00:05:41.463 --> 00:05:44.089
it's so amazing when we
get to team up for arts ed,

00:05:44.089 --> 00:05:44.972
because -

00:05:44.972 --> 00:05:46.621
- I was just about to
say that, that segue.

00:05:46.621 --> 00:05:50.570
It, art is so important.
People don't get it.

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:52.130
Even if you don't become a singer

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.921
or a professional
musician, it's so important

00:05:53.921 --> 00:05:56.688
for your character, your
team building skills.

00:05:56.688 --> 00:05:58.214
And just like sports in that sense, and -

00:05:58.214 --> 00:05:59.047
- Yeah.

00:05:59.047 --> 00:06:00.634
- And it's just, and to
be a part of something,

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:03.377
I think to find your kind
of group, like in school.

00:06:03.377 --> 00:06:04.210
- Absolutely.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.043
- It's also important art.

00:06:05.043 --> 00:06:05.876
The arts are so important for school.

00:06:05.876 --> 00:06:06.709
- Yeah.

00:06:06.709 --> 00:06:07.542
And when you realize that
sports is not your thing,

00:06:07.542 --> 00:06:09.107
yeah, the arts is right there for you.

00:06:09.107 --> 00:06:12.509
I have, it's great when the math shows you

00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:14.832
how well it does in schools, you know.

00:06:14.832 --> 00:06:17.866
It isn't about finding
the next star, you know.

00:06:17.866 --> 00:06:18.699
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:18.699 --> 00:06:20.176
- It's about leadership skills
and confidence building.

00:06:20.176 --> 00:06:22.616
Graduation rates go up.
Home life gets better.

00:06:22.616 --> 00:06:23.449
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:24.282
- So -

00:06:24.282 --> 00:06:25.774
- People find a purpose,
and they find, yeah.

00:06:25.774 --> 00:06:27.604
I totally agree.

00:06:27.604 --> 00:06:30.074
- And right now, especially,
when young people, you know,

00:06:30.074 --> 00:06:32.621
are in and out of school because of COVID,

00:06:32.621 --> 00:06:35.342
they're looking at our world
leaders, they're looking at,

00:06:35.342 --> 00:06:38.263
you know, the world at large
and they're full of conflict.

00:06:38.263 --> 00:06:40.377
They're full of questions, full of fear.

00:06:40.377 --> 00:06:42.458
And the arts, you know,

00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:44.479
is a way to unlock a
lot of that confusion,

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:45.753
a lot of those questions in a way

00:06:45.753 --> 00:06:47.759
that makes the world
around them much clearer,

00:06:47.759 --> 00:06:50.022
much more empathetic, and -

00:06:50.022 --> 00:06:51.648
- And if it's done right,
it explains it to them.

00:06:51.648 --> 00:06:52.481
- It explains it.

00:06:52.481 --> 00:06:54.656
- Without, yeah, without punching
them in the face with it.

00:06:54.656 --> 00:06:55.724
- [Josh] Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:06:55.724 --> 00:06:56.725
- 'Cause it's hard with kids.

00:06:56.725 --> 00:06:59.864
But, so Josh also did
musical theater as a kid.

00:06:59.864 --> 00:07:01.146
We both actually did.

00:07:01.146 --> 00:07:02.114
Not many people know this,

00:07:02.114 --> 00:07:04.943
but Josh was a guest on the
pilot episode of this show

00:07:04.943 --> 00:07:06.494
because he's super cool and nice

00:07:06.494 --> 00:07:08.635
and totally came and did me a solid.

00:07:08.635 --> 00:07:11.179
But we talked about our
musical theater backgrounds,

00:07:11.179 --> 00:07:13.451
and we realized something
strange as we talked.

00:07:13.451 --> 00:07:14.906
Take a look.

00:07:14.906 --> 00:07:15.739
I remember thinking, though,

00:07:15.739 --> 00:07:17.285
when I first was introduced
to musical theater,

00:07:17.285 --> 00:07:19.141
oh, we're just all cool
with like, they're just,

00:07:19.141 --> 00:07:20.759
she's just gonna break out in song, like,

00:07:20.759 --> 00:07:21.601
as if it's normal?

00:07:21.601 --> 00:07:22.434
- [Josh] Oh, yeah.

00:07:22.434 --> 00:07:23.322
- Like, she's just, like talking, and -

00:07:23.322 --> 00:07:24.164
- That's the thing, right, right.

00:07:24.164 --> 00:07:26.238
- I'm feeling a song, so
I'm just going to do that?

00:07:26.238 --> 00:07:27.415
I kind of thought that was awkward.

00:07:27.415 --> 00:07:28.737
- It is awkward, and
people who are sometimes

00:07:28.737 --> 00:07:29.781
a little weird about -

00:07:29.781 --> 00:07:32.300
♪ Is it me ♪

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:37.300
♪ Or is it just the way he smiles
that leaves me breathless ♪

00:07:38.049 --> 00:07:40.852
♪ How can I not tell her ♪

00:07:40.852 --> 00:07:43.188
♪ That I love her ♪

00:07:43.188 --> 00:07:45.088
- So, like Idina Menzel. That is crazy.

00:07:45.088 --> 00:07:46.682
- Yes, crazy, right?

00:07:46.682 --> 00:07:50.265
- Crazy. You got to
tour with Idina Menzel.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:51.996
- [Josh] We're -

00:07:51.996 --> 00:07:53.799
- I mean, she got to tour Josh Groban.

00:07:53.799 --> 00:07:55.581
- No, no, no, we are about
to hit the road together.

00:07:55.581 --> 00:07:56.664
She is truly.

00:07:57.652 --> 00:07:58.485
- Oh, you're about to -

00:07:58.485 --> 00:07:59.318
- We're about to hit the road.

00:07:59.318 --> 00:08:00.151
- I thought just did.

00:08:00.151 --> 00:08:01.255
- No, no, we're about to do it.

00:08:01.255 --> 00:08:02.139
No, she's just unbelievable.

00:08:02.139 --> 00:08:04.014
You know it, you know how
it is. I mean, she's just

00:08:04.014 --> 00:08:09.014
♪ And all at once, my life
starts to have meaning ♪

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:16.090
♪ And all at once I can't ever look back ♪

00:08:18.459 --> 00:08:19.318
- But crazy that y'all

00:08:19.318 --> 00:08:21.560
are going to be there the same
time, right, 'cause, like -

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.393
- Same time.

00:08:22.393 --> 00:08:23.995
- You're going to get to
sing "Let It Go," possibly.

00:08:23.995 --> 00:08:24.828
- "Let It Go."

00:08:24.828 --> 00:08:26.740
Well, I don't know, I mean,
she sings "Let It Go,"

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.590
and I just listen.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:30.310
- Yeah. I would like to
hear you sing "Let It Go."

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:31.910
- I would like to hear
myself sing "Let It Go,"

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:32.743
but you know what?

00:08:32.743 --> 00:08:34.149
Sometimes you just got
to let those dreams go.

00:08:34.149 --> 00:08:36.006
- Do you sometimes sing
"Let It Go" in the shower?

00:08:36.006 --> 00:08:37.597
- In the shower. Best reverb of all time.

00:08:37.597 --> 00:08:39.266
♪ I finally found him ♪

00:08:39.266 --> 00:08:41.470
♪ I finally found her ♪

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:44.470
♪ And I'll never be ♪

00:08:46.667 --> 00:08:47.848
- It is so great to talk to you.

00:08:47.848 --> 00:08:48.873
- I just adore you.

00:08:48.873 --> 00:08:49.957
- You're so awesome.

00:08:49.957 --> 00:08:51.790
I totally forgot that.

00:08:52.844 --> 00:08:56.011
♪ I also forgot ♪

00:08:56.011 --> 00:08:57.636
I love you so much for doing that.

00:08:57.636 --> 00:08:59.777
I just remembered, after watching that,

00:08:59.777 --> 00:09:02.782
he literally learned that
right before we did it.

00:09:02.782 --> 00:09:06.133
Like we put that together
right before we did it.

00:09:06.133 --> 00:09:07.447
And you were so game.

00:09:07.447 --> 00:09:08.624
- Well, you only gave me one line.

00:09:08.624 --> 00:09:09.705
I mean, it was really, it was -

00:09:09.705 --> 00:09:10.640
- [Kelly] Whatever.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:13.690
- Look, you've graduated from stools to,

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:14.694
look at that beautiful couch.

00:09:14.694 --> 00:09:16.282
- And look, and I have a band now,

00:09:16.282 --> 00:09:17.115
like a full band.

00:09:17.115 --> 00:09:17.948
- [Josh] Oh my gosh.

00:09:17.948 --> 00:09:18.781
- It's all amazing.

00:09:18.781 --> 00:09:19.781
Look what you helped me accomplish.

00:09:19.781 --> 00:09:20.614
- [Josh] Oh, no listen -

00:09:20.614 --> 00:09:21.447
- You did this, Groban.

00:09:21.447 --> 00:09:24.010
- It was an honor to be
there then, and it is now.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:24.843
- Oh my God. All right.

00:09:24.843 --> 00:09:26.700
Well, your new album is called "Harmony."

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:29.520
Is there a theme to it,
other than maybe harmony?

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:30.832
- This was an interesting process.

00:09:30.832 --> 00:09:31.904
Yeah, I mean, we called it "Harmony"

00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:32.815
for a couple of reasons.

00:09:32.815 --> 00:09:34.487
One, obviously the musical connotations,

00:09:34.487 --> 00:09:36.762
but also just the incredible moving parts

00:09:36.762 --> 00:09:39.980
and effort that had to go into
making an album right now.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:40.813
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:40.813 --> 00:09:42.816
- You know, this is the
weirdest, hardest experience

00:09:42.816 --> 00:09:44.866
I've ever had making an
album, and it's because

00:09:44.866 --> 00:09:46.133
we obviously had to do it safely.

00:09:46.133 --> 00:09:48.012
We had musicians from all over the world

00:09:48.012 --> 00:09:49.517
that had to be separated

00:09:49.517 --> 00:09:52.157
and had to take different
time outs in order to be safe.

00:09:52.157 --> 00:09:54.727
And so, you know, I've never made an album

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:55.927
this virtual, you know.

00:09:55.927 --> 00:09:57.739
It's like, we're seeing
your audience here.

00:09:57.739 --> 00:09:59.011
We had string players in London

00:09:59.011 --> 00:10:00.744
while our producer was in Nashville.

00:10:00.744 --> 00:10:01.777
- Especially artists like you,

00:10:01.777 --> 00:10:03.890
because you always have the
kind of big orchestral elements.

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:05.036
- I'm pretty, I was lucky

00:10:05.036 --> 00:10:06.617
that I got to be raised pretty old school

00:10:06.617 --> 00:10:09.374
in this business where
like, you're the, you know,

00:10:09.374 --> 00:10:10.603
you're in the room with the group,

00:10:10.603 --> 00:10:12.797
and you don't want to be the
bum note of all the 60 people.

00:10:12.797 --> 00:10:13.756
You're doing it all together.

00:10:13.756 --> 00:10:14.589
- Yeah.

00:10:14.589 --> 00:10:16.623
- And so, we couldn't do
it that way this time.

00:10:16.623 --> 00:10:20.439
And so, in order to make,
you know, it come together,

00:10:20.439 --> 00:10:22.762
we had to do it, you know,
from all over the world.

00:10:22.762 --> 00:10:25.519
And so, that's, in many ways,

00:10:25.519 --> 00:10:28.148
this is the most special and
unique process that I've had

00:10:28.148 --> 00:10:30.006
because being able to make this album

00:10:30.006 --> 00:10:32.288
and being able to sing songs
that have felt so relevant

00:10:32.288 --> 00:10:33.515
to the times we're in,

00:10:33.515 --> 00:10:35.620
these songs have been such classics

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:38.571
and they remain the
soundtracks to our lives,

00:10:38.571 --> 00:10:40.289
has just meant so, so much to me.

00:10:40.289 --> 00:10:42.519
So I feel very, very, very grateful

00:10:42.519 --> 00:10:43.894
that I got to sing a little bit this year

00:10:43.894 --> 00:10:45.855
and got to release an album
that means a lot to me.

00:10:45.855 --> 00:10:47.918
- All right. Well, Josh
will be performing "Angels"

00:10:47.918 --> 00:10:49.505
for us later in this show.

00:10:49.505 --> 00:10:51.736
You can get his new
album, "Harmony," out now,

00:10:51.736 --> 00:10:53.121
and head to his website for info

00:10:53.121 --> 00:10:55.408
on his virtual holiday concert

00:10:55.408 --> 00:10:58.662
that takes place December 19th,
his first holiday concert,

00:10:58.662 --> 00:11:00.616
which I'm kind of still
mad about, but it's fine.

00:11:00.616 --> 00:11:01.449
- [Josh] Make it a good one.

00:11:01.449 --> 00:11:02.617
- We, and it's going
to be, better be good.

